This fixture exercises phpc's MySQLi statement result-binding handle
validation through a WordPress-shaped `wpdb` method. System PHP would require
a real mysqli statement object, by-reference result binding, result buffer
mutation, and fetch integration; phpc only records the reached
non-statement-object diagnostic here. Supported placeholder statement result
binding is covered in later fixtures and does not implement true
by-reference aliasing, unbuffered statement fetching, bound-parameter
execution, real mysqlnd cursor behavior, or host database state.
